# API Testing with REST Client (VS Code)
# This file allows you to verify your microservices manually.

@gateway_url = http://localhost:3000
@auth_url = http://localhost:3001
@target_email = user@example.com
@target_password = SecurePassword123

### 
### 1. HEALTH CHECK: GATEWAY (The "Front Door")
GET {{gateway_url}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

### 
### 2. HEALTH CHECK: AUTH SERVICE (The "Backbone")
GET {{auth_url}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

### 
### 3. SIGNUP (Creates a real user in Neon PostgreSQL)
# @name signup
POST {{auth_url}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{target_email}}",
    "password": "{{target_password}}",
    "name": "Jane Doe"
}

### 
### 4. LOGIN (Returns a JWT token)
# @name login
POST {{auth_url}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{target_email}}",
    "password": "{{target_password}}"
}

### 
### 5. EXTRACT TOKEN (Requires running Step 4 first)
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 
### 6. GET ME (Caches profile in Redis after the first request)
GET {{auth_url}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 
### 7. CREATE RAZORPAY ORDER (Razorpay Integration)
POST {{gateway_url}}/api/v1/payments/create-order
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "amount": 500,
    "currency": "INR",
    "receipt": "order_rcpt_11"
}

### 
### 8. FILE UPLOAD (Media Service - Multer + Cloudinary)
# Replace with a real local file path if testing via VS Code REST Client
POST {{gateway_url}}/api/v1/media/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="profile.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/test-image.jpg
--boundary--
